      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-323730",
      ":question/problem": "Consider quadratic function $g(x) = ax^{2} + 6x + c$, where $a$ and $c$ are constants. The graph of $y = g(x)$ in the $xy$-plane is a parabola that opens upward and has a vertex at the point $(h, k)$, where $h$ and $k$ are constants. If $k < 0$ and $g(-8) = g(4)$, which of the following **MUST** be true?\n\n1. $c < 0$\n2. $a > 0$\n3. $c > 0$"
    },
